native x64 (SysV): a cross-package multi-return whose component is a managed interface value (@errors.Error) is miscompiled — same family as the aa64 xfail (the @Iface tuple component is mis-sized in the multi-return ABI), here crashing when strconv.ParseInt etc. return (T, @errors.Error). Codegen-level, so both x64-linux (ELF) and x64-darwin (Mach-O) hit it; not funcval-related (the big-multi-return-x64 fix f0747762 doesn't touch it). See claude-todo.md (native managed-iface multi-return).
